# Never commit the corpus itself
library/
*.pdf
*.epub

# Secrets
.env
*.env

# Run state and logs
*.log
*.jsonl
*checkpoint*.json
.raptor-baseline.json
.search-circuit-state.json

# ...but the evaluation query sets are committed deliberately. They are the
# yardstick: a score is only comparable to another score measured against the
# identical set, so the set has to travel with the code that reports the number.
!eval/queries-*.jsonl

# The REAL query set and its judgments are deliberately NOT published. They are
# extracted from a private search history, so the file is a list of what someone
# actually looked for and which books they own. eval_real_set.py regenerates an
# equivalent set from any deployment's own logs, which is the point -- the
# harness is the artifact, not one person's reading list.
eval/real-queries.jsonl
eval/qrels-real.jsonl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
